apt 2.7.14 cmake: use SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIRS (plural) in methods dir

The apt-internal FindSECCOMP.cmake module exports the variable
SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIRS (plural), but methods/CMakeLists.txt referenced the
singular form ${SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIR}, which is never defined, so
include_directories(...) in the methods directory received an empty list
and every compile in methods/ failed with:

  methods/aptmethod.h:31:10: fatal error: 'seccomp.h' file not found

On a distro Linux build /usr/include happens to hold seccomp.h, so the
empty include list is harmless and the bug is invisible.  On a cross
build (OHOS) the conan prefix include dir is only reachable through
SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIRS and the build fails.

Fix by using the plural variable, matching what FindSECCOMP.cmake
actually exports.
--- a/methods/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/methods/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 # Create the executable targets
-include_directories($<$<BOOL:${SECCOMP_FOUND}>:${SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIR}>)
+include_directories($<$<BOOL:${SECCOMP_FOUND}>:${SECCOMP_INCLUDE_DIRS}>)
 link_libraries(apt-pkg $<$<BOOL:${SECCOMP_FOUND}>:${SECCOMP_LIBRARIES}>)
 
 add_library(connectlib OBJECT connect.cc rfc2553emu.cc)

